The active profile is `spring-data-jpa` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/application.properties` line 20: `spring.profiles.active=h2,spring-data-jpa`). The active implementation is the Spring Data proxy `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` (`@Profile("spring-data-jpa")`, extends `OwnerRepository, Repository<Owner, Integer>`). It does NOT override `save`, so `save` is Spring Data's default `SimpleJpaRepository.save` — i.e. `persist` for a new entity (id null) and `merge` otherwise. No custom save logic.

For reference, the non-active `@Profile("jpa")` implementation `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` (lines 92-100) makes the new-vs-existing behavior explicit:

```java
@Override
public void save(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.getId() == null) {
        this.em.persist(owner);
    } else {
        this.em.merge(owner);
    }
}
```

